        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Ferrari, Lancia, Banana Republic, Victoria's Secret, Forever 21, Dolce & Gabbana, Louis Vuitton, Diesel, Gucci, Prada, Ferrari Store, Burberry, Fendi, Hugo Boss\n- Places: Beverly Center, Maranello, Joan's on Third, La Cienega Boulevard, Farmer's Market at the Grove, Fairfax Avenue\n- Products: Lancia LC2\n- Topics: retail tenants, sports car manufacturing, racing cars\n\nFacts:\n- As of 2017, Beverly Center included tenants such as Banana Republic, Victoria's Secret, Forever 21, Dolce & Gabbana, Louis Vuitton, Diesel, Gucci, Prada, Ferrari Store, Burberry, Fendi, and Hugo Boss.\n- Ferrari N.V. is an Italian sports car manufacturer based in Maranello.\n- Joan's on Third is located in an area popular with Angelenos for eating and shopping, between Beverly Center on La Cienega Boulevard and Farmer's Market at the Grove on Fairfax Avenue.\n- The Lancia LC2, sometimes called the Lancia-Ferrari, was a series of racing cars built by Lancia and powered by engines built by its sister company Ferrari.",
